# Compose interpolation template, NOT an API env file and NOT deploy approval.
# Copy outside the repository, chmod 0600, and supply via --env-file explicitly.
# Every referenced credential file must also be private and outside the checkout.
# Do not paste credentials into chat, commit them, or publish resolved compose
# output: compose config may render env_file secrets. Use config --quiet instead.
# Requires Docker Compose >=2.30 for env_file format: raw (literal secret values).

ODDPATH_API_IMAGE=oddpath-api:closed-rehearsal
ODDPATH_MIGRATION_IMAGE=oddpath-api-migrations:closed-rehearsal
# Host loopback port only; use 0 for a disposable test's ephemeral port.
ODDPATH_API_PORT=5000
# Pin reviewed image digests before any live release; tags alone are mutable.
ODDPATH_POSTGRES_IMAGE=postgres:16-alpine
ODDPATH_POSTGRES_VOLUME=oddpath-rehearsal-pg16
ODDPATH_POSTGRES_PASSWORD_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/postgres-admin-password
ODDPATH_API_ENV_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/api.env
ODDPATH_MIGRATION_ENV_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/migration.env

# REQUIRED ROLE CONTRACT -- provision before starting API/migrations:
# - A fresh dedicated PG16 volume/instance, never a production/restored user DB.
# - Database oddpath; schema/migration owner oddpath_migrator, LOGIN with separate
#   password, NOSUPERUSER NOCREATEDB NOCREATEROLE NOREPLICATION.
# - oddpath_runtime: separate LOGIN/password, NOSUPERUSER NOCREATEDB NOCREATEROLE
#   NOREPLICATION, CONNECT only to oddpath, USAGE on its application schema,
#   SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on application tables and USAGE/SELECT on their
#   sequences; no schema CREATE, ownership or membership in oddpath_migrator.
# - Grant those table/sequence rights AFTER controlled migrations, plus matching
#   ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES FOR ROLE oddpath_migrator IN SCHEMA public for later
#   migrations. Revoke PUBLIC CREATE and unnecessary PUBLIC database privileges.
#   Exclude _prisma_migrations from runtime write privileges; it is migration
#   metadata, not an application table. Verify this after broad/default grants.
# - Do not set API DATABASE_URL to postgres or to the schema-owner credential.
# - The PG bootstrap password file contains only the high-entropy admin password;
#   only the postgres service mounts it. An empty volume may initialize postgres,
#   but this compose NEVER provisions application roles or grants automatically.
#   Missing app roles/schema must fail; do not solve it by using the admin role.
# - Bootstrap/role SQL is an explicit operator action on this dedicated instance.

# API ENV FILE CONTENT (create at ODDPATH_API_ENV_FILE; remove comment prefixes):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://oddpath_runtime:<URL-encoded-password>@postgres:5432/oddpath?schema=public
# APP_ORIGIN=https://oddpath.eluthira.com
# CORS_ORIGIN=https://oddpath.eluthira.com
# CSRF_SECRET=
# USAGE_IP_HASH_SALT=
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=smtp
# EMAIL_FROM=Oddpath <no-reply@eluthira.com>
# SMTP_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# EMAIL_OUTBOX_ENCRYPTION_SECRET=
# AUTH_EMAIL_RESPONSE_FLOOR_MS=350
# PASSWORD_RESET_PATH=/#/reset-password
# EMAIL_VERIFICATION_PATH=/#/verify-email
# AUTH_TOKEN_RETENTION_DAYS=7
# UNVERIFIED_ACCOUNT_RETENTION_DAYS=7
# USAGE_RECORD_RETENTION_DAYS=32
# RETENTION_CLEANUP_BATCH_SIZE=100
# USAGE_WINDOW_HOURS=24
# AI_GLOBAL_USAGE_WINDOW_MS=3600000
#
# Blank secrets intentionally prevent production boot. Generate independent
# high-entropy CSRF/IP-salt/mail-encryption secrets >=32 characters, and fill the
# actual SMTP credentials. raw env files use literal values: no shell quoting or
# variable interpolation. URL-encode DB credentials. Never reuse DB/admin/SMTP
# passwords as application signing/encryption keys.
# Feature gates in compose deliberately override this file: registration, AI,
# browser/v2/manual/saved login, private assets, imports and QA workers stay off.
# No R2, provider, browser viewer, vault keyring or Docker credentials are needed
# for this closed slice. It is not the accepted public-beta feature set.

# MIGRATION ENV FILE CONTENT (ODDPATH_MIGRATION_ENV_FILE; no API/SMTP secrets):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://oddpath_migrator:<different-URL-encoded-password>@postgres:5432/oddpath?schema=public
#
# Explicit order after dedicated volume/role bootstrap and image builds:
# 1. Start only postgres; verify it is the isolated intended DB.
# 2. Run the operations-profile migrate service once; require exit code 0.
#    Never use migrate dev/reset/db push and never auto-migrate on API startup.
# 3. Apply/recheck runtime grants, then start API. Its SELECT 1 readiness probe
#    is not evidence of schema migration completion or Phase 08 acceptance.
# 4. Host proxy remains a separate gate: one trusted hop only, replacing forwarded
#    IP/proto headers. Keep port 5000 loopback-only and Cloudflare DNS-only until
#    ingress/TLS/cookies/CSRF/rate limits are independently exercised.
# 5. Retention/reconciliation, alerts, encrypted off-host backups with seven-day
#    retention and a restore drill must be added/rehearsed before real user data.
#    Preserve quota policy consistently for API and maintenance; do not purge
#    accounting holds or reset Stop/revocation journals to make recovery pass.
#
# This slice has no browser services or vault volumes. When separately activated,
# API+API reaper need the SAME durable revocation journal; runtime supervisor+
# runtime reaper need their own shared journal. Keys remain separate and private.
# Do not add them by mounting Docker.sock/keyrings into this API or tenant images.
# No Oracle resource, DNS, certificate, backup uploader, paid service or deployment
# is created by these files. Actual ARM safety/capacity and live operations remain
# NOT VERIFIED. Keep staging/production/rehearsal volumes and credentials separate.

# OPTIONAL local operations overlay (see PHASE_08A_READINESS_INVENTORY.md).
# Supply ALL overlay interpolation values when selecting that additional file;
# omit the file entirely for the unchanged base closed rehearsal.
# ODDPATH_OPERATIONS_IMAGE=oddpath-operations:reviewed
# ODDPATH_MAINTENANCE_STATE_VOLUME=oddpath-maintenance-state
# ODDPATH_BACKUP_STATE_VOLUME=oddpath-backup-state
# ODDPATH_ENCRYPTED_BACKUP_VOLUME=oddpath-encrypted-backups
# ODDPATH_BACKUP_ENV_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/backup.env
# ODDPATH_BACKUP_KEY_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/backup-key
# ODDPATH_BACKUP_PGPASS_FILE=/etc/oddpath-rehearsal/backup.pgpass
#
# Pre-provision those volumes: private0700, owned by the operations image's
# postgres UID (inspect the exact image; do not assume host UID). No Docker.sock.
# Key: independent random 32-byte key encoded as 64 lowercase hex characters,
# mode0600 and readable by that UID. Back up the key SEPARATELY from archives.
# pgpass: postgres:5432:oddpath:oddpath_backup:<distinct-password>, mode0600.
# Backup env contains ONLY PGHOST=postgres, PGPORT=5432, PGDATABASE=oddpath,
# PGUSER=oddpath_backup, PGSSLMODE=disable for this private local network.
# No DATABASE_URL, admin, migrator, SMTP, LLM or API signing secrets.
# oddpath_backup: LOGIN NOSUPERUSER NOCREATEDB NOCREATEROLE NOREPLICATION;
# CONNECT oddpath, USAGE public, SELECT application tables/sequences and migration
# history; matching SELECT-only default privileges under oddpath_migrator.
# No INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/CREATE/TEMP or membership in owner/runtime roles.
# Local Compose file secrets are bind-backed: mode0600/ownership must be correct
# on the HOST. Container mode attributes do not repair an unsafe source file.
#
# Maintenance inherits the SAME API env/window/retention policy. Usage runs each
# minute, retention every15min, object deletion every5min whenever all R2 creds
# are configured (even when upload flags are off). Partial storage config fails.
# Backups run at startup when due, then daily, verified with seven-day retention.
# Maintenance uses a DB session advisory lock; backup uses an OS-backed SQLite
# lock on its private LOCAL volume, so hourly archive pruning survives DB/key
# outages. Never put this lock on network storage or manually replace it live.
# Both retain durable status and bounded alerts;
# health fails on failed/incomplete/stale runs. No external notification is sent.
# This database-only slice REFUSES runtime/saved-login/asset data. Full encrypted
# journal/key/object backup integration remains required before enabling them.
# These local volumes are NOT an off-host backup. Live off-host copy, alert
# delivery, restore/revocation/deletion/accounting continuity remain release gates.
